\p
\v 43 Then Yahweh¦31384 told Mosheh¦31387 and Aharon¦31388, “This¦31389 is¦31390 the statute¦31390 of¦31390 the ‘pass-over¦31391’: No foreigners¦31396 may \add share in\add* the meal \add that night\add*,
\v 44 unless it's a slave¦31404 that you¦31409 bought and¦31409 who's been circumcised¦31409—
\v 45 no foreigner or hired¦31416 helper can \add join in\add* the meal.
\v 46 \add Each animal\add* must¦31425 be eaten¦31425 in only one house—don't take any of the meat¦31434 outside¦31435. And don't break¦31438 any of the animals bones¦31436.\x + \xo 12:46: \xt Num 9:12; Yhn 19:36.\x*
\v 47 Every¦31445 Israeli¦31444 must¦31446 observe it¦31447,
\v 48 and if someone is living among you¦31452 and wants to join in Yahweh's¦31456 ‘pass-over¦31455’, then every¦31459 male¦31461 in their family must¦31451 be circumcised¦31457. Only then will they be allowed to observe¦31464 it, and then they should be considered like¦31466 a native¦31466 of¦31466 the¦31467 land¦31467. No uncircumcised¦31470 person may eat¦31473 it.
\v 49 This one¦31477 law will¦31478 apply to both the natives¦31479, and¦31480 those who¦31481 live among¦31482 you¦31482 all.”
\v 50 All¦31492 the¦31487 Israelis¦31488 followed those instructions¦31490 that Yahweh¦31491 had¦31490 given through Mosheh¦31494 and¦31495 Aharon¦31497,
\v 51 and¦31502 \add so\add* on¦31503 that¦31505 very day¦31504, Yahweh¦31507 took all the Israelis¦31511 out¦31506 of Egypt¦31513 \add grouped\add* by their¦31516 \add family\add* divisions.
\c 13
\s1 God owns the first child
