\p
\v 1 Then Yahweh¦31520 told Mosheh¦31523,
\v 2 “All¦31537 firstborn¦31531 \add offspring\add* are to be consecrated to me—the first product of every¦31533 womb¦31535, whether human¦31538 or animal, belongs to me.”\x + \xo 13:2: \xt Num 3:13; Luk 2:23.\x*
\s1 The ‘Flat Bread Celebration’
\rem /s1 The Festival of Unleavened Bread
\p
\v 3 Then¦31543 Mosheh¦31544 told the people¦31547, “\add Always\add* remember¦31548 this day¦31551, that¦31552 you went¦31554 out of Egypt¦31555, \add rescued\add* from slavery¦31557, because¦31558 Yahweh¦31562 \add ≈used his power\add* to bring¦31561 you out from there. And¦31565 \add ≈nothing with¦31559 yeast in¦31559 it¦31566\add* can be¦31566 eaten¦31566 \add when you celebrate this\add*.
\v 4 Today you¦31570 are¦31571 leaving in¦31572 the¦31572 month¦31572 of¦31572 Aviv,
\v 5 and \add when\add* Yahweh¦31579 brings¦31578 you into¦31580 the \add ≈area occupied by\add* the Canaanites¦31583, Hittites¦31584, Amorites¦31585, Hivites¦31586, and the Yebusites¦31587 (which¦31588 he¦31589 swore¦31589 to your¦31590 fathers¦31590 to give¦31591 to you—a land¦31593 flowing¦31594 with¦31602 milk¦31595 and honey¦31596) you must¦31578 observe¦31597 this ceremony¦31600 in¦31602 this \add same\add* month¦31602.
\v 6 You¦31607 must¦31607 eat¦31607 \add only\add* flat bread¦31608 for seven days¦31606, and¦31609 then on¦31609 the seventh¦31610 day¦31609, there will be a festival¦31611 to¦31612 \add honour\add* Yahweh¦31612.
\v 7 \add Again,\add* you must only eat flat bread for¦31622 seven¦31617 days¦31618—\add not only that\add* you mustn't \add even have\add* any risen bread, nor must you have any yeast within any of¦31631 your¦31631 borders.
\v 8 On that¦31636 \add festival\add* day¦31635, you¦31633 must¦31633 tell¦31633 your¦31634 \add children\add*, ‘This is because of¦31638 what¦31639 Yahweh¦31641 did¦31640 for \add us\add* when¦31643 \add we left\add* Egypt¦31644.’
\v 9 It'll¦31664 be \add ≈like a reminder¦31652 written\add* on your hand and¦31646 \add ≈hanging from your forehead\add*, so¦31655 that¦31655 \add ≈you'll remember to pass on\add* Yahweh's¦31658 instructions because¦31660 \add *he¦31663\add* \add ≈used his power\add* to bring¦31663 you out¦31663 of Egypt¦31665.
\v 10 \add So\add* you¦31667 must¦31667 \add ≈follow those instructions\add* at the appointed¦31672 time¦31672 \add ≈year after year\add*.
\s1 Offering up the oldest children
