\p
\v 11 Later¦31678, when Yahweh¦31681 brings¦31680 you into¦31682 the land¦31684 of¦31684 the Canaanites¦31685 as¦31686 he promised to you and your¦31689 ancestors¦31689, and he gives¦31690 it¦31690 to you,
\v 12 then¦31693 hand over to Yahweh all \add your\add* oldest \add ≈sons\add*, and¦31700 all the¦31704 oldest, male animal offspring that¦31706 are yours¦31708. They will¦31707 \add then\add* belong¦31707 to Yahweh.\x + \xo 13:12: \xt Exo 34:19-20; Luk 2:23.\x*
\v 13 In the case of the oldest donkey foal, you must buy it back \add by killing a lamb\add* instead of it. If¦31718 you don't¦31720 buy it back, you must kill the donkey by breaking¦31722 its¦31722 neck¦31722. You \em must\em* buy back every¦31723 one of your¦31726 oldest sons¦31726,
\v 14 and¦31729 \add ≈in the future¦31734\add* when your¦31733 son¦31733 asks¦31732 you, ‘What's¦31736 that¦31738 about?’ then¦31729 you must¦31732 tell him, ‘\add ≈We were enslaved in Egypt¦31745, but¦31729 Yahweh¦31744 used his incredible power\add* to bring¦31743 us¦31743 out¦31743.
\v 15 And so it¦31749 was that when Far'oh¦31753 was too stubborn¦31752 to let¦31754 us¦31754 go¦31754, then¦31749 Yahweh struck all of the oldest sons and oldest male animals in Egypt¦31761. That's why \add we\add* offer all the oldest offspring to Yahweh, and why \add we need to buy back\add* all our oldest sons.’
\v 16 \add So\add* you must place a reminder on your hand and¦31785 hanging on your forehead that Yahweh¦31797 used his incredible power to bring¦31796 us¦31796 out¦31796 of Egypt¦31798.”
\s1 Led by cloud and fire
\rem /s1 Crossing the Sea; The Pillars of Cloud and Fire; The Pillar of Cloud and the Pillar of Fire; Israel's Wilderness Detour
\p
\v 17 When¦31802 Far'oh¦31803 released the people, God¦31810 didn't¦31807 lead¦31809 them¦31809 through the \add ≈area occupied by\add* the Philistines¦31813, although \add @that way¦31811\add* was¦31815 shorter, because¦31814 \add *he\add* said¦31819, “\add ≈It's best if the people don't¦31807 have to face¦31825 war immediately, or they¦31825 might change their minds\add* and¦31827 \add then want to\add* return¦31827 to Egypt¦31828.”
\v 18 \add So\add* God¦31831 caused¦31830 the people to take the path¦31836 going towards the wilderness¦31837 and¦31830 the Red Sea.\f + \fr 13:18 \ft Probably towards the \+em Gulf of Suez\+em*: see https://armstronginstitute.org/339-where-did-the-red-sea-crossing-take-place.\f* The Israeli¦31845 left Egypt¦31847 \add ≈in formation as if ready for battle¦31841\add*.
\p
\v 19 Mosheh¦31850 \add ensured that\add* Yosef's¦31854 bones were taken with \add them\add*, because¦31856 \add many years back\add* \add @Yosef\add* had¦31858 made¦31858 the¦31861 Israelis¦31862 promise, saying¦31863, “God¦31866 will certainly take notice of¦31871 you all, and¦31868 you must¦31865 take my¦31871 bones \add ≈out\add* from¦31872 here¦31872 with you.”\x + \xo 13:19: \xt Gen 50:25; Josh 24:32.\x*
\p
\v 20 The people travelled on from¦31876 Succoth¦31876 and¦31877 camped¦31877 at¦31878 Etham¦31878 on the edge¦31879 of¦31879 the wilderness¦31880.
\v 21 During the day¦31885, Yahweh¦31882 went ahead of them in a pillar of cloud¦31887 to lead them on¦31886 the way, and at nighttime, he went in a pillar of fire¦31892 to be light¦31893 to them, \add so they could travel both\add* in the daytime and at night¦31897.
\v 22 The¦31902 daytime pillar of cloud¦31903 and¦31905 the nighttime¦31907 pillar of fire¦31906, didn't ever leave their place \add ≈ahead\add* of the people¦31909.
\c 14
\s1 Crossing the Red Sea
\rem /s1 Crossing the Red Sea
\p
\v 1 Then Yahweh¦31913 told Mosheh¦31916,
\v 2 “Tell the Israelis¦31923 that¦31924 they¦31924 should turn¦31924 and camp in front of Pi-Hahirot, between¦31929 Migdol¦31930 and the sea, in front of Baal-Zephon¦31935. You all are to camp by the sea opposite¦31936 it¦31936.
\v 3 Then¦31942 Far'oh¦31943 will say, ‘They¦31945 are¦31946 confused¦31946 \add and lost\add*—the wilderness¦31951 has¦31949 boxed them in.’
\v 4 I'll strengthen Far'oh's \add ≈resolve\add* and he'll chase after¦31960 them¦31960. Then¦31953 because¦31968 of¦31965 Far'oh and all¦31963 his¦31965 army¦31965, I'll be \add honoured\add* and the Egyptians will¦31966 know¦31966 that¦31968 I am¦31971 Yahweh¦31971.” \add ≈So¦31953 the Israelis camped where they¦31972 were instructed\add*.
\rem /s1 The Egyptians Pursue Israel
\p
\v 5 When¦31976 the king¦31977 of Egypt¦31978 was told¦31976 that¦31992 the Israelis¦31981 had¦31980 fled¦31980, \add *he\add* and his¦31985 servants¦31985 \add started thinking about their own\add* people¦31988 and they¦31989 asked, “What¦31990 have¦31993 we done¦31993 by letting the Israeli slaves go¦31996 free?”
\v 6 Then¦32002 he¦32009 hitched up his chariot¦32005 and¦32006 took¦32009 his \add army\add* with¦32010 him¦32010.
\v 7 He¦32012 took¦32012 600 of the best chariots as well as all¦32018 the other Egyptian¦32020 chariots and¦32012 officers¦32021 \add to supervise\add* them.
\v 8 Yahweh¦32027 strengthened the Egyptian¦32039 king's¦32032 resolve and¦32026 so Far'oh¦32031 pursued¦32034 after the Israelis¦32037 after they had confidently marched out \add of Egypt\add*.
\v 9 The Egyptians pursued¦32044 them, then¦32044 all of Far'oh's horses¦32055 and chariots¦32056, along with his mounted soldiers and his foot army¦32059, overtook¦32047 them camping above the¦32064 sea¦32052 above Pi-Hahirot, across from Baal-Zephon¦32066.
\p
\v 10 As \add the Egyptians\add* approached, the Israelis¦32073 looked back, and \add to their horror\add*, saw the army coming after¦32081 them¦32081. They¦32082 were¦32082 extremely afraid¦32082 and cried¦32084 out¦32084 to Yahweh¦32090.
\v 11 They¦32092 \add complained\add* to Mosheh¦32095, “Is it because¦32096 there¦32097 weren't any graves¦32099 in Egypt that¦32106 you brought¦32101 us here to die¦32102 in the wilderness¦32103? What¦32104 have¦32107 you done¦32107 to us? Why did you bring¦32109 us out¦32109 from¦32110 Egypt?
\v 12 Isn't this¦32114 \add exactly what we told\add* you¦32118 in Egypt¦32119 when we said¦32120, ‘\add ≈Just leave us alone\add* and let us serve¦32123 the Egyptians’? Because¦32127 serving¦32130 the Egyptians \add sounds a lot\add* better to¦32129 us than¦32134 dying¦32134 \add out here\add* in the wilderness¦32135.”
\p
\v 13 Then¦32137 Mosheh¦32138 told the¦32141 people¦32141, “You mustn't be¦32144 afraid¦32144. Stand¦32145 still and¦32137 see how Yahweh¦32150 saves you all—he's going to do¦32142 it today, because¦32156 any Egyptians that¦32151 you see today, you'll never, ever see them¦32165 again¦32166.
\v 14 Yahweh¦32171 himself will¦32172 fight¦32172 for you all—all you need to do is to remain calm.”
\rem /s1 Escape through the Red Sea
\v 15 Then Yahweh¦32179 \add scolded\add* Mosheh¦32182, “Why¦32183 are¦32185 you¦32185 \add still here\add* crying¦32185 out¦32185 to me¦32186? Talk to the¦32190 Israelis¦32192 and¦32178 get them moving forward¦32193.
\v 16 As for you, raise¦32196 your staff¦32199 and stretch¦32200 your arm out over¦32204 the sea and divide¦32207 it¦32207. Then¦32195 the Israelis¦32211 will go¦32208 on¦32214 onto dry ground¦32214 through the middle¦32212 of the sea.
\v 17 \add Yes, watch me!\add* I'll strengthen the resolve of the Egyptians and they'll enter \add between the sea\add* after¦32224 them¦32224. Then¦32216 I'll be honoured¦32225 because of \add what will happen to\add* Far'oh¦32226 and all¦32227 his army¦32229, and his chariots¦32230 and his horsemen¦32231.
\v 18 ⇔The honour¦32239 that I gain¦32239 \add ≈through that will¦32233 cause\add* the Egyptians to know¦32233 that I'm Yahweh¦32238.”
\p
\v 19 Then¦32244 God's¦32246 messenger¦32245 who¦32247 travelled ahead of the Israelis¦32250, moved and went¦32251 behind them. \add Also\add* the pillar¦32254 of cloud¦32255 moved from in front¦32248 of them and stood¦32257 behind them
\v 20 and \add so\add* it was then¦32260 between¦32261 the \add coming\add* Egyptians and the Israelis¦32267. Then¦32260 the cloud¦32269 became darkness¦32270 \add on the Egyptian side\add*, \add yet it lit up the other side\add*, and no one could approach it all¦32282 night¦32284.
\v 21 Then¦32286 Mosheh¦32287 stretched¦32286 his arm out over¦32291 the sea and Yahweh¦32295 sent a strong¦32302 east¦32301 wind¦32301. It blew all¦32303 night¦32305 and divided¦32311 the sea \add on each side\add* and dried the \add strip of\add* land in¦32300 the middle.
\v 22 \add So\add* then¦32314 the Israelis¦32317 entered through the middle¦32318 of the sea¦32319 on dry ground¦32320 with¦32320 a wall¦32323 of water¦32321 on each side of them.\x + \xo 14:22: \xt 1Cor 10:1-2; Heb 11:29.\x*
\v 23 \add However,\add* the Egyptians pursued¦32327 after¦32330 them¦32330. Every¦32331 one of Far'oh's horses and chariots¦32334 and his¦32335 horsemen¦32335 \add also\add* entered into¦32336 the middle¦32338 of the sea¦32339.
\v 24 \add By now morning was coming\add* and Yahweh¦32345 looked¦32344 down¦32344 through the pillar¦32350 of fire¦32351 and cloud¦32352, and he¦32353 caused confusion¦32353 for the Egyptian¦32356 army.
\v 25 He¦32358 caused¦32358 the wheels¦32360 of their¦32361 chariots¦32361 to turn¦32358 unevenly \add so they became difficult\add* to drive¦32362, and the Egyptians \add complained\add*, “Let's¦32366 retreat from¦32367 \add following\add* the Israelis¦32367, because¦32369 Yahweh¦32370 is¦32371 fighting¦32371 against¦32373 Egypt¦32365 and for¦32372 them¦32372.”
