\p
\v 26 \add On the other side,\add* Yahweh¦32377 told Mosheh¦32380, “Stretch¦32381 your¦32384 arm out¦32381 over¦32385 the sea¦32387 and the waters¦32389 will \add flow back\add* onto the Egyptians and onto \add @Far'oh's\add* chariots¦32395 and his horsemen¦32398.”
\v 27 \add So\add* Mosheh¦32401 stretched¦32400 his arm out over¦32405 the sea, and as the day broke, the sea began to return¦32408 to its normal¦32412 place. The Egyptians \add turned and\add* fled¦32414 before¦32415 its impact \add but\add* Yahweh¦32417 shook¦32416 the Egyptians \add off their horses and chariots\add* in¦32421 the middle¦32421 of the sea.
\v 28 \add So\add* the sea returned¦32424 and covered¦32426 the chariots¦32429 and the horsemen¦32432—even Far'oh's entire army¦32434 that had entered into the sea after¦32437 \add @the Israelis\add*. Not¦32439 even one¦32445 of¦32434 \add @the pursuers\add* remained¦32441.
\v 29 \add But\add* the \add ≈Israelis¦32448\add* had walked¦32449 through the middle¦32451 of the sea¦32452 on dry ground¦32450 with¦32450 a wall¦32455 of water¦32453 \add ≈on each side of them\add*.
\p
\v 30 \add So\add* Yahweh¦32460 saved¦32459 Yisrael¦32465 from Egypt's¦32467 power that day¦32461, and¦32459 the Israelis saw¦32468 the Egyptians' bodies \add washed up\add* on¦32474 the shore¦32476.
\v 31 \add All\add* \add ≈the Israelis¦32480\add* saw¦32479 the \add ≈incredible power¦32483\add* that¦32485 Yahweh had¦32486 used against the Egyptians, and the people¦32490 revered Yahweh, and put their trust in¦32488 him and his¦32497 servant¦32497 Mosheh¦32496.
\c 15
\s1 Mosheh's song
\rem /s1 The Song of Moses; A Song of Deliverance; The Song of Moses and Miriam
\p
\v 1 Then¦32500 Mosheh¦32503 and¦32504 the¦32519 Israelis¦32505 sang¦32501 this¦32509 song¦32508 to¦32514 Yahweh:\x + \xo 15:1: \xt Rev 15:3.\x*
\q1 “I will¦32513 sing¦32513 to Yahweh because¦32515 he's been so successful—
\q1 he's thrown¦32521 both the horses¦32519 and their riders¦32520 into the sea¦32522.
\q1
\v 2 I will¦32533 sing about Yahweh¦32526, my¦32524 source of¦32524 strength¦32525,\x + \xo 15:2: \xt Psa 118:14; Isa 12:2.\x*
\q2 and¦32536 the one who saves me.
\q1 I will praise¦32533 him¦32533 because he's¦32527 my god—
\q1 ≈he's my father's¦32535 god¦32532 and I will honour¦32533 him.
\q1
\v 3 Yahweh is a warrior.
\q1 Yahweh is his¦32542 name¦32542.
\b
\q1
\v 4 He threw Far'oh's chariots¦32544 and his army¦32546 into the¦32549 sea¦32548.
