\q1
\v 9 Our enemies thought that they could chase after us and overtake¦32600 us.
\q1 They had planned to satisfy themselves by sharing out the plunder¦32602.
\q1 They were ready to use their swords¦32606 and swing their arms to destroy¦32607 us.
\q1
\v 10 \add But\add* you blew¦32610 with¦32611 your¦32611 breath¦32611.
\q1 The sea¦32613 covered¦32612 them.
\q1 They¦32614 sank¦32614 like¦32615 lead¦32615 in¦32611 that \add ≈terrible surge\add*.
\b
\q1
\v 11 Which other god is¦32621 like¦32621 you¦32621, Yahweh¦32623?
\q1 Who¦32624 else is so powerful and yet sinless,
\q2 receiving praises¦32629 for doing¦32630 miracles?
