\v 18 Yahweh¦32706 will¦32708 reign¦32708 \add as king\add* forever and¦32710 ever¦32710.
\q1
\v 19 Far'oh's¦32715 horse went¦32713 into the sea¦32731, along with¦32716 his¦32716 chariots¦32716 and¦32717 horsemen¦32717,\f + \fr 15:19 \ft Some interpreters include v19 as part of¦32727 Mosheh's song (as we do, although it does seem less poetic in structure), while others don't. (There's no speech marks in the ancient Hebrew texts.)\f*
\q1 and Yahweh¦32720 brought¦32719 the¦32714 water¦32724 back¦32719 over¦32721 them¦32721,
\q1 \add after\add* the Israelis¦32727 had walked¦32728 through on¦32716 dry ground¦32729 in¦32716 the middle¦32730 of the sea.”
\s1 Miryam's song
