\p
\v 20 Then Aharon's¦32738 sister¦32737 Miryam who was a prophetess¦32736, picked up a tambourine¦32741 and went¦32743 outside. All the other women¦32746 did likewise and followed her¦32742 out to dance together
\v 21 \add so\add* Miryam¦32753 sang¦32751 this response:
\q1 “Sing¦32754 to Yahweh¦32755 and¦32761 tell of¦32761 his amazing victory—
\q1 He¦32762 tossed the horses¦32760 and their riders¦32761 into the sea¦32763.”
\s1 The bitter water
\rem /s1 Bitter Water; In the wilderness; The Waters of Marah and Elim; Bitter Water Made Sweet; Bitter Water at Marah
\p
\v 22 Then Mosheh¦32767 lead¦32766 the Israelis away from¦32771 the Red Sea¦32771 and they¦32774 moved into¦32775 the wilderness at¦32784 Shur¦32779. They¦32780 went¦32780 through the wilderness for three¦32781 days¦32783 and \add finally\add* found¦32787 some water¦32788,
\v 23 but¦32790 it was so bitter that they couldn't drink¦32794 it. So¦32790 they named that place ‘Marah¦32791’ \add (which means ‘bitter’)\add*,
\v 24 and¦32808 the¦32809 people¦32809 grumbled¦32808 about Mosheh¦32812 saying¦32813, “\add So\add* what¦32814 will¦32816 we¦32816 drink¦32816 \add then\add*?”
\v 25 \add So\add* Mosheh cried¦32818 out¦32818 to Yahweh, and¦32835 Yahweh showed¦32822 him¦32822 a tree¦32824. When¦32818 he threw¦32825 it into¦32826 the water, the water became¦32829 \add safe to drink\add*.
\p \add @Yahweh\add* made¦32832 a statue at that place, and a rule, and he tested¦32837 \add @Mosheh\add* there,
\v 26 saying¦32839, “If¦32840 you carefully¦32842 listen to the voice¦32844 of Yahweh your god¦32847, and you do¦32850 what's right¦32848 in¦32849 my eyes¦32849, and you listen to my commands¦32852 and you keep¦32853 all¦32854 of my laws, then¦32839 I won't¦32864 inflict you with¦32849 any¦32857 of the diseases¦32859 that¦32860 I put on¦32849 the Egyptians, because¦32868 I'm Yahweh your healer.”
\p
\v 27 \add Then they moved on\add* and came¦32874 to Elim¦32875 where there were twelve springs¦32879 and seventy¦32881 palm¦32882 trees¦32882, and they camped¦32883 there by the¦32888 water¦32880.
\c 16
\s1 The manna and the quail
\rem /s1 Manna and Quail; Manna and Quail from Heaven; Bread from Heaven; The Manna and the Quails
\p
\v 1 Then¦32890 they¦32890 left¦32890 Elim, and all¦32893 the Israelis¦32898 entered into the wilderness¦32901 at¦32910 Siyn (between¦32905 Elim and Sinai¦32909) \add ≈around six weeks\add* after¦32915 leaving Egypt¦32917,
\v 2 and all¦32921 the Israelis¦32926 murmured against¦32930 Mosheh¦32929 and Aharon¦32932 \add there\add* in¦32933 the wilderness¦32933,
\v 3 saying¦32935, “If¦32938 only \add ≈Yahweh¦32945 had¦32958 killed us\add* in¦32943 Egypt¦32947, \add where we'd be\add* sitting¦32948 by¦32943 a pot¦32951 of meat¦32952 eating¦32953 bread until we're full, because¦32956 you've brought¦32958 us out into¦32960 this¦32963 wilderness¦32962 to \add ≈starve us all¦32967 to death¦32964\add*.”
\p
\v 4 Then Yahweh¦32975 told Mosheh¦32978, “\add Just\add* watch me make food¦32982 rain¦32980 down¦32980 from the sky for you all. Then the people¦32987 will be able to go¦32986 out every day and gather¦32988 enough for that day so¦32993 that I can test¦32994 them: Will¦32995 they¦32988 obey my¦32996 law¦32996 or¦32997 not?\x + \xo 16:4: \xt Yhn 6:31.\x*
\v 5 \add ≈But¦33001 every Friday¦33005\add* they can \add gather and\add* prepare¦33004 twice as much as what they gather on the other days.”
\p
\v 6 \add So\add* Mosheh¦33021 and Aharon¦33022 told all the Israelis¦33028, “This evening¦33029 you'll all know¦33030 that¦33031 Yahweh¦33032 was the one who brought¦33033 you out¦33033 from¦33035 Egypt¦33036.
\v 7 In the¦33042 morning¦33038 you'll all see¦33039 Yahweh's¦33043 greatness as he's¦33044 heard¦33044 your¦33047 murmurings against \add *him\add*. \add I mean,\add* who are¦33051 we¦33051 that you'd murmur against \em us\em*?”
\v 8 Then¦33058 Mosheh¦33059 continued¦33058, “So¦33058 Yahweh will give¦33060 you all meat¦33064 to eat¦33065 in the evening¦33063 and¦33058 enough bread¦33066 in the morning¦33067 to make you all full. \add Yes,\add* Yahweh has¦33069 heard¦33069 your murmurings against him¦33078. As for us, \add ≈we're insignificant\add*. Your murmuring isn't¦33081 against us, but¦33058 against Yahweh.”
\p
\v 9 Then¦33090 Mosheh¦33091 told Aharon¦33094, “Summon¦33102 everyone¦33101 to come and¦33090 face¦33104 Yahweh¦33105, because¦33106 he's¦33107 heard¦33107 their murmurings.”
\v 10 And¦33126 so while Aharon¦33113 spoke¦33112 to¦33114 all¦33116 the Israelis¦33121, they¦33122 turned¦33122 toward the wilderness¦33125, and¦33111 wow, Yahweh's¦33128 \add dazzling brightness\add* appeared¦33129 in¦33130 the cloud¦33130!
\v 11 Then Yahweh¦33134 told Mosheh¦33137,
\v 12 “I've¦33140 heard¦33140 the murmurings of¦33143 the Israelis¦33145. Speak¦33146 to¦33147 them¦33147 saying¦33148, ‘In the evenings¦33150, you'll all eat¦33151 meat¦33152, and¦33153 in¦33153 the mornings¦33153 you'll all be¦33154 satisfied¦33154 with¦33153 bread¦33156. Then you'll all know¦33157 that¦33158 I'm your god¦33161, Yahweh¦33160.’ ”
\p
\v 13 And so that evening¦33164, quail¦33166 appeared and¦33163 covered¦33167 the camp. And in¦33164 the morning¦33171, \add something like\add* dew¦33174 was lying all around¦33175 the camp,
\v 14 and¦33178 when it evaporated, wow, it left behind thin flakes¦33187—thin like¦33189 frost¦33189 on¦33190 the ground there in the wilderness¦33185.
\v 15 \add When\add* the¦33195 Israelis¦33197 saw¦33194 it, \add ≈they asked each¦33199 other\add*, ‘What¦33203 is¦33204 it?’ because¦33205 they didn't¦33206 know¦33207 what¦33208 it was.
\p And¦33211 Mosheh¦33212 told them¦33213, “It's¦33214 the food¦33215 that¦33216 Yahweh¦33218 has¦33217 given¦33217 you all to¦33219 eat.\x + \xo 16:15: \xt 1Cor 10:3.\x*
\v 16 \add ≈These are¦33238 Yahweh's¦33226 instructions¦33225\add*: Gather¦33227 enough of¦33238 it¦33228 according to¦33230 how many people¦33235 you're feeding—about two litres per person¦33235 who¦33237 lives in¦33238 your¦33235 tents.”
\p
\v 17 \add So\add* the¦33244 Israelis¦33245 went ahead and gathered¦33246 it—some collecting a lot, and others, less,
\v 18 \add but\add* when they¦33250 measured¦33250 it out, those who'd collected a lot didn't¦33252 have any extra, and¦33250 those who hadn't gathered so much still had enough to¦33259 eat—each person had gathered just enough.\x + \xo 16:18: \xt 2Cor 8:15.\x*
\v 19 Then¦33264 Mosheh¦33265 told them¦33266, “Don't¦33268 save any of it¦33271 for tomorrow,”
\v 20 \add but some of\add* them didn't¦33276 take any notice of him and kept it until¦33285 the next morning¦33287. However¦33293, by then¦33276 it was full of maggots and smelt rotten¦33288, and Mosheh¦33281 was very angry¦33291 at them.
\p
\v 21 \add So from that day onwards,\add* they gathered¦33295 it¦33296 every¦33299 morning, depending on¦33297 how many they were feeding, and¦33295 then¦33295 when the sun¦33303 got hot, \add @the rest\add* melted¦33304 \add away\add*.
\v 22 On the \add ≈Friday\add*, they¦33310 gathered¦33310 twice as much—around \add four litres\add* for¦33315 each person—and all¦33317 the leaders of¦33317 the community came¦33316 and informed Mosheh
\v 23 and he¦33324 told them¦33325, “This is what Yahweh said¦33328: Tomorrow¦33335 is a rest day to be set aside for¦33334 Yahweh. \add ≈So¦33324 bake or cook your food, and keep¦33352 the left-overs overnight to use in\add* the morning¦33355.”\x + \xo 16:23: \xt Exo 20:8-11.\x*
\v 24 \add So\add* they¦33357 did what Mosheh¦33364 had¦33363 told¦33363 them and kept the left-overs until¦33359 the morning¦33361, and it didn't¦33365 stink¦33366 or have any bugs in¦33371 it.
\v 25 On that Saturday morning, Mosheh¦33374 told them, “Go ahead and eat¦33375 the previously cooked food because¦33377 today is¦33379 set aside for¦33381 Yahweh¦33381 and so you all won't¦33383 find¦33384 any more \add on the ground\add*—
\v 26 you'll gather¦33389 it¦33389 for six days¦33388 \add each week\add*, but¦33390 on¦33390 the¦33391 Saturday, there won't¦33393 be¦33394 any.”
\p
\v 27 \add However,\add* some people¦33404 did go¦33401 out to¦33405 collect it, but¦33398 they¦33407 couldn't find¦33407 any,
\v 28 and Yahweh¦33411 said¦33410 to Mosheh¦33414, “For how long will you¦33418 all keep refusing¦33418 to obey my commands¦33420 and my laws¦33421?
\v 29 Listen, Yahweh¦33426 has¦33427 given¦33427 you the Rest Day¦33436, so¦33432 on the Friday he¦33433 gives¦33434 you food¦33438 for two¦33439 days¦33439. On the Saturday, everyone¦33442 should¦33446 stay where they are—there's¦33430 no need for anyone¦33447 to go¦33446 outside \add searching\add*.”
\v 30 So¦33452 the people¦33453 didn't work on the Saturday.
\p
\v 31 The¦33458 Israelis¦33460 named it ‘manna¦33464’ \add (which sounds like Hebrew ‘What is it?’)\add*. It was white¦33468 like coriander¦33467 seed¦33466, and¦33457 it tasted¦33469 like wafers¦33470 with¦33471 honey¦33471.\x + \xo 16:31: \xt Num 11:7-8.\x*
\v 32 Then¦33473 Mosheh¦33474 said¦33473, “This¦33475 is¦33476 the procedure that Yahweh¦33479 has¦33478 commanded¦33478: Keep a full measure of¦33480 it¦33482 for preservation for your descendants so¦33485 that they¦33487 can see¦33487 the food¦33490 which¦33491 I fed you in¦33494 the wilderness¦33494, when¦33495 I brought¦33495 you out¦33495 from¦33497 Egypt¦33498.”
\v 33 \add So\add* Mosheh¦33501 said¦33500 to Aharon¦33504, “Take¦33505 a jar¦33506 and¦33500 fill it with the full two litres of manna¦33514. Place¦33515 it in¦33517 front¦33517 of Yahweh¦33518 for preservation for your descendants.”\x + \xo 16:33: \xt Heb 9:4.\x*
\v 34 \add So\add* Aharon¦33529 \add prepared the jar and kept it\add* (and would \add eventually\add* place¦33528 it \add in the box\add* with the \add stone tablets\add*.)
\v 35 The Israelis¦33535 ate¦33536 manna¦33539 for forty¦33540 years, until¦33542 they¦33544 \add eventually\add* \add ≈left the wilderness\add* and¦33534 came¦33555 to¦33556 the borders¦33558 of the region¦33547 of Canaan¦33560.\x + \xo 16:35: \xt Josh 5:12.\x*
\v 36 (Two litres is called an ‘omer¦33562’ which is a tenth¦33563 of¦33563 a ‘efah’.)
\c 17
\s1 Yahweh gives water from a rock
\rem /s1 Water From the Rock; Water from the Rock
\r (Num. 20:1-13)
\p
\v 1 Then all¦33569 the Israelis¦33574 moved on¦33584 from¦33575 Siyn in¦33584 the wilderness¦33575, travelling following Yahweh's¦33582 instructions. They¦33583 camped¦33583 at¦33584 Refidim¦33584 \add but\add* there¦33585 was¦33585 no water¦33586 for the people¦33588 to drink¦33587.\x + \xo 17:1-7: \xt Num 20:2-13.\x*
\v 2 \add So\add* the¦33591 people¦33591 argued with¦33592 Mosheh¦33594 \add again\add*, saying, “Give¦33596 us¦33598 water¦33599 to¦33602 drink¦33600!”
\p “Why are you all quarrelling¦33590 with me¦33607?” Mosheh \add ≈answered\add*. “Why are you all testing Yahweh¦33613?”
\p
\v 3 \add But\add* the people were \add very\add* thirsty there¦33616 and \add *they\add* murmured against Mosheh¦33623, \add so\add* he¦33624 \add demanded\add*, “Is this¦33626 why you brought¦33627 us¦33627 out of Egypt¦33628? To¦33625 kill me¦33630 and my sons and my cattle with¦33637 thirst¦33637?” ???
\p
\v 4 Mosheh¦33640 cried¦33639 out¦33639 to Yahweh¦33643, \add asking\add*, “What¦33645 should I do¦33646 for \add ^these\add* people¦33647? \add ≈It won't take much more\add* and¦33651 they'll \add ≈kill¦33651\add* me¦33651.”
\p
\v 5 “Walk on¦33673 ahead of the people¦33660,” Yahweh¦33654 told Mosheh¦33657, “and take¦33661 some of the Israeli¦33663 elders¦33663 with you, and your staff¦33665—the one which¦33666 you struck¦33667 the river with. Take¦33672 it in¦33673 your hand¦33673 and go¦33674.
\v 6 Watch me. I will stand¦33677 \add ≈in¦33684 front¦33678 of you\add* there¦33679 on¦33684 the rock at¦33684 Horev \add !(Mt. Sinai)\add*. Then you will strike¦33685 the rock and water¦33689 will come¦33687 out¦33687 of it¦33688, and the people¦33691 will drink¦33690.” \add So\add* Mosheh¦33694 did that while the Israeli¦33696 elders¦33696 watched.
\p
\v 7 \add @Mosheh\add* named that place¦33701 \add both\add* ‘Massah¦33702’ \add (which means ‘testing’)\add* and ‘Meribah¦33703’ \add (which means ‘complaining’)\add*, because of the conflict among the Israelis¦33709 and because of how they¦33711 tested¦33711 Yahweh by saying¦33715, ‘Is Yahweh among us or¦33719 not¦33721?’
\s1 Mosheh's arms held high to defeat Amalek
\rem /s1 The Amalekites Defeated; Israel Defeats the Amalekites; Amalek Attacks Israel and Is Defeated; War with the Amalekites
\p
\v 8 Then the Amalek¦33725 \add army\add* came¦33724 and attacked Yisrael¦33729 at¦33730 Refidim¦33730,
\v 9 and Mosheh¦33733 instructed Yehoshua¦33736 \add !(Joshua¦33736)\add*, “Choose¦33737 men¦33740 for¦33739 us¦33739 and go¦33741 out¦33741 and fight¦33742 with Amalek¦33743. Tomorrow¦33744 I'll¦33745 be¦33746 stationed on¦33743 top¦33749 of the hill¦33750 with the staff¦33751 of God¦33752 in¦33743 my¦33753 hand¦33753.”
