\v 3 along with \add #their\add* two¦33907 sons¦33908. One¦33911 was¦33912 named ‘Gershom¦33912’ \add (which sounds like the Hebrew word for ‘foreigner’)\add* because¦33913 \add @Mosheh\add* had¦33914 said¦33914, “I've¦33916 been a foreigner living in¦33917 another country.”\x + \xo 18:3: \xt Acts 7:29.\x*
\v 4 \add Their\add* other son's name¦33920 was¦33922 ‘Eliezer¦33922’ \add (which sounds like the Hebrew word that means ‘God helps me’\add*, because¦33923 Mosheh had said, “God, who my¦33927 father¦33926 worshipped, has¦33928 helped me and¦33928 \add ≈stopped the Egyptian king Far'oh¦33930 from killing me\add*.”))
\p
