\v 11 and¦34570 be¦34570 prepared¦34571 for¦34572 the third day, because¦34574 on the third day \add *I\add* will¦34578 come¦34578 down¦34578 to¦34580 Mt¦34579. Sinai¦34587 while all¦34581 the people¦34583 watch.
\v 12 Set¦34589 boundaries¦34589 for¦34589 the people¦34592 all¦34593 around¦34593, and¦34599 tell \add <them\add*, ‘Don't climb on¦34598 the mountain¦34598 or touch¦34599 its¦34600 edge¦34600, because anyone¦34603 who¦34603 does will¦34606 definitely be¦34606 executed.\x + \xo 19:12-13: \xt Heb 12:18-20.\x*
\v 13 Anyone \add who touches the mountain\add* mustn't be touched by anyone else—they must¦34610 be \add ≈executed by throwing rocks¦34615 at¦34629 them\add* or shooting them \add with a bow\add*. No person or animal¦34623 \add who touches the mountain\add* can stay alive.’ \add ≈Only after a long¦34629 trumpet blast¦34629\add* should they \add start to\add* climb the mountain.”
\v 14 \add So\add* Mosheh¦34636 went down the mountain¦34639 to¦34640 the people. He¦34644 purified them and¦34635 they¦34647 \add all\add* washed¦34647 their¦34648 clothes¦34648,
