\v 18 Yahweh¦34711 descended onto Mt¦34720. Sinai¦34704 \add surrounded\add* by fire¦34712 and the entire¦34706 mountain smoked. Its¦34706 smoke went up like¦34715 the smoke from a furnace¦34716, and the whole¦34706 mountain trembled¦34717 violently.
\v 19 Then¦34723 it happened \add after\add* the sound¦34724 of the horn¦34725 got extremely loud, that Mosheh¦34729 was speaking¦34730 and¦34723 God¦34731 was answering¦34732 him¦34732 in¦34733 a voice¦34733.
\v 20 Yahweh¦34736 had descended¦34735 onto the top of Mt¦34739. Sinai¦34740, and¦34735 \add *he¦34745\add* called¦34745 Mosheh up to the top of the mountain¦34751, \add so\add* Mosheh ascended¦34752.
\v 21 \add But\add* Yahweh¦34756 told \add *him\add*, “Go¦34760 \add back\add* down¦34760 and warn¦34761 the people¦34762 in¦34762 case they¦34765 force their way through¦34765 to look at¦34762 \add *me\add* and many¦34772 of them perish¦34770.
\v 22 Also¦34774, the¦34775 priests¦34775 who¦34776 come¦34776 nearer to \add *me\add*, they¦34780 \add ≈must¦34780 be very careful to purify themselves¦34780\add* in¦34784 case \add *I\add* \add ≈suddenly punish\add* them¦34784.”
\v 23 \add But\add* Mosheh¦34788 \add questioned\add* Yahweh¦34791, “The¦34795 people¦34795 aren't¦34792 able¦34794 to come¦34796 up¦34796 on¦34805 Mt¦34799. Sinai¦34800, because¦34801 you yourself warned¦34804 us,\x + \xo 19:23 \xt 19:12.\x* ‘Set¦34807 boundaries¦34807 all around the mountain¦34810 to keep it¦34811 sacred.’ ”
\v 24 “Go \add back\add* down¦34818,” Yahweh¦34815 \add ≈responded¦34813\add*, “and bring Aharon¦34821 back up with¦34836 you. \add However,\add* the priests¦34823 and the people¦34824 \add ≈must¦34819 not¦34825 cross the boundary\add* to come¦34828 up to \add *me\add*, in¦34836 case \add *I\add* \add ≈suddenly punish\add* them¦34836.”
\v 25 \add So\add* Mosheh¦34839 went down and¦34843 spoke to¦34840 the¦34842 people¦34842.
\c 20
\s1 The ten rules
\rem /s1 The Ten Commandments
\r (Deu. 5:1-22)
\p
\v 1 Then God¦34848 \add ≈gave these¦34853 instructions\add* \add to the Israelis\add*:
\v 2 I'm¦34857 your¦34860 god¦34860 Yahweh¦34859, who¦34862 \add ≈rescued you\add*\f + \fr 20:2 \ft Although modern English doesn't easily distinguish it, this discourse is addressed to singular ‘you’, i.e., to the Israelis as one group. While some of our modern, individualistic cultures might naturally interpret these rules as applying to individuals, they were given to Yisrael/Israel to implement at a national level.\f* \add ≈from where you were enslaved in\add* Egypt¦34865.
\li1
\v 3 You mustn't own any other¦34879 gods¦34877 \add ≈in my¦34883 sight\add*.
\li1
\v 4 You¦34888 mustn't make¦34888 a carved figure for¦34890 yourself¦34890, nor \add carve a copy\add* of anything in the sky above¦34903 or in the earth below, or that's in the water¦34914 under¦34916 the earth.\x + \xo 20:4-5: \xt Exo 34:17; Lev 19:4; 26:1; Deu 4:15-18; 27:15.\x*
\v 5 Don't¦34922 bow¦34924 down¦34924 to¦34927 \add @idols\add* and don't¦34922 serve¦34930 them¦34930, because¦34932 I, your¦34935 god¦34935 Yahweh¦34934, am a jealous¦34937 God¦34935. I remember the sins of the fathers¦34940 and \add punish\add* the children¦34943 of \add even\add* the third¦34946 and fourth¦34949 \add generation\add* of those¦34950 who¦34950 hate¦34950 me,\x + \xo 20:5-6: \xt Exo 34:6-7; Num 14:18; Deu 7:9-10.\x*
\v 6 \add but\add* I \add ≈faithfully fulfil my promises\add* to¦34957 \em thousands¦34957\em* \add of generations\add* of those¦34959 who love¦34959 me¦34959 and¦34960 who obey my instructions.
\li1
\v 7 You¦34976 mustn't \add ≈wrongly promote\add* the¦34968 name¦34968 of Yahweh¦34970 your¦34971 god¦34971, because¦34973 \add *I¦34974\add* won't¦34964 leave¦34975 anyone unpunished¦34975 who¦34978 \add ≈does that\add*.\x + \xo 20:7: \xt Lev 19:12.\x*
\li1
\v 8 \add ≈Keep Saturday different from all the other days\add*\x + \xo 20:8: \xt Exo 16:23-30; 31:12-14.\x*—
\v 9 there's six¦34999 days¦35001 \add every week\add* for working¦35009.\x + \xo 20:9-10: \xt Exo 23:12; 31:15; 34:21; 35:2; Lev 23:3.\x*
\v 10 The¦35013 seventh¦35014 day is¦35016 a rest day for¦35018 Yahweh¦35018 your god¦35019: you mustn't do¦35023 any¦35025 work¦35027—not you, or your children, or your male¦35035 or female¦35037 servants¦35037, or your cattle, or the foreigners \add ≈living among you\add*—
\v 11 because¦35049 Yahweh¦35054 made the heavens¦35057 and earth¦35060, the sea¦35063, and everything that's in them¦35070 in six¦35050 days¦35052. Then¦35078 he rested¦35071 on¦35070 the seventh¦35073 day, so¦35076 that's why \add *he\add* blessed¦35077 the rest day and made it¦35083 sacred¦35083.\x + \xo 20:11: \xt Gen 2:1-3; Exo 31:17.\x*
\li1
\v 12 Honour¦35089 your father¦35089 and¦35090 your mother¦35092, so¦35093 that \add ≈you'll have a long¦35094 life\add* on¦35096 the¦35097 land that your god¦35101 Yahweh¦35100 is¦35102 about¦35102 to give¦35102 you.\x + \xo 20:12: a \xt Deu 27:16; Mat 15:4; 19:19; Mrk 7:10; 10:19; Luk 18:20; Eph 6:2; \xo b \xt Eph 6:3.\x*
\li1
\v 13 You¦35108 mustn't murder¦35108.\x + \xo 20:13: \xt Gen 9:6; Lev 24:17; Mat 5:21; 19:18; Mrk 10:19; Luk 18:20; Rom 13:9; Jam 2:11.\x*
\li1
\v 14 You¦35114 mustn't commit¦35114 adultery¦35114.\x + \xo 20:14: \xt Lev 20:10; Mat 5:27; 19:18; Mrk 10:19; Luk 18:20; Rom 13:9; Jam 2:11.\x*
\li1
\v 15 You¦35120 mustn't steal¦35120.\x + \xo 20:15: \xt Lev 19:11; Mat 19:18; Mrk 10:19; Luk 18:20; Rom 13:9.\x*
\li1
\v 16 You¦35126 mustn't \add ≈lie in¦35127 court\add*.\x + \xo 20:16: \xt Exo 23:1; Mat 19:18; Mrk 10:19; Luk 18:20.\x*
\li1
\v 17 You mustn't covet your¦35147 neighbour's¦35147 house¦35134 or spouse, or their male¦35141 or female¦35142 servants, or their animals, or anything else they own.\x + \xo 20:17: \xt Rom 7:7; 13:9.\x*
\s1 The people are afraid of God
