\p
\v 18 All¦35150 of the people¦35152 could hear and see the thunder¦35156 and the lightning¦35159, the sound¦35161 of the horn¦35162, and the mountain¦35165 smoking¦35166. They trembled¦35169 \add when\add* \add *they\add* saw¦35167 it, and they \add remained\add* standing¦35170 at a distance¦35171.\x + \xo 20:18-19: \xt Heb 12:18-19.\x*
\v 19 They¦35173 \add begged\add* Mosheh¦35176, “You be the one to speak to us, and¦35173 we'll listen¦35181, but¦35173 don't¦35182 let¦35184 God¦35186 speak \add directly\add* to us, in case we die¦35189.”
\p
\v 20 “Don't¦35202 be¦35198 afraid¦35198,” Mosheh¦35192 responded¦35191, “because¦35199 God¦35204 has¦35203 come¦35203 to¦35200 test¦35201 you so that the fear¦35207 of¦35207 him \add ≈will¦35212 remain with¦35200 you\add* so that you all won't¦35196 \add ≈disobey him\add*.”
\v 21 So¦35214 the people¦35215 stood¦35214 \add ≈at a good distance¦35216\add* \add while\add* Mosheh¦35217 approached toward the thick¦35221 darkness¦35221 where¦35222 God¦35225 was¦35224.
\s1 Instructions about altars
