\p
\v 22 Then Yahweh told Mosheh¦35232, “This is what you need to¦35235 tell the¦35237 Israelis¦35238: ‘You yourselves have seen¦35240 that¦35241 I, \add Yahweh,\add* have talked with¦35246 you from heaven¦35244.
\v 23 You all mustn't make¦35249 gods out of silver¦35252 or gold¦35254 for¦35257 yourselves¦35257 to have alongside¦35250 me.
\v 24 You¦35261 need to make¦35261 an altar¦35259 for¦35263 me¦35263 out of dirt, and then you can sacrifice¦35264 your burnt¦35268 offerings and peace¦35271 offerings, and your sheep¦35274 and cattle¦35277, on it. \add ≈I'll inform you about every place¦35280 where¦35281 I want to be¦35282 worshipped\add* and I'll come¦35286 to you and will¦35288 bless¦35288 you \add there\add*.
\v 25 If¦35300 you do make¦35294 me an¦35292 altar¦35292 with stones, you mustn't use cut stones to build¦35299 it because¦35302 moving your¦35303 tools over it will defile it.\x + \xo 20:25: \xt Deu 27:5-7; Josh 8:31.\x*
\v 26 And don't¦35308 use steps¦35311 to get up¦35310 to the altar¦35314 because you¦35310 might expose your \add ≈private parts\add* \add under your robes\add*.
\c 21
