\m \add @Those¦40866 craftsmen\add* must¦40867 make everything \add exactly\add* according¦40863 to¦40863 my instructions¦40866.
\s1 The rest day
\rem /s1 Instructions for the Sabbath; The Sabbath; Sabbath, the Day of Rest; The Sabbath Law
\p
\v 12 Then Yahweh¦40871 told Mosheh¦40874:
\v 13 Tell the Israelis¦40882 that you all must¦40888 certainly observe¦40888 the \add weekly\add* rest day because¦40889 \add @the rest day\add* is¦40890 a sign¦40890 between¦40892 me¦40892 and¦40893 you all throughout¦40894 your¦40899 generations¦40894, so that you will¦40888 know¦40895 that I am¦40898 Yahweh¦40898, who¦40899 \add ≈wants to distinguish you from other nations\add*.
\v 14 \add So\add* you all must observe¦40901 the rest day because¦40905 it's¦40907 sacred¦40906 for¦40908 you. Anyone who \add ≈treats it as an ordinary day\add* must be put¦40911 to¦40911 death¦40911. Anyone who works¦40917 on¦40916 it must be \add ≈expelled from¦40921 the community\add*.
\v 15 There's¦40933 six days¦40925 for working, and¦40928 then the seventh¦40929 is a rest day—\add ≈dedicated\add* to \add *me\add*. Anyone¦40936 who¦40936 works on¦40928 it¦40926 must¦40926 certainly be¦40941 put¦40941 to death¦40941.\x + \xo 31:15: \xt Exo 20:8-11; 23:12; 34:21; 35:2; Lev 23:3; Deu 5:12-14.\x*
\v 16 The¦40944 Israelis¦40946 must¦40943 observe¦40943 the¦40949 rest day for¦40950 all future generations¦40954. There's no ending to¦40954 this agreement¦40955
\v 17 between¦40959 me¦40958 and the Israelis¦40961. It's¦40970 a never-ending sign¦40962 that \add *I\add* made¦40969 the heavens¦40973 and the earth¦40976 in¦40977 six¦40967 days¦40968, and then rested¦40979 on¦40977 the seventh¦40978 day¦40977 and was refreshed¦40980.\x + \xo 31:17: \xt Exo 20:11.\x*
\rem /s1 The Two Tablets of the Covenant
\p
\v 18 When \add @Yahweh\add* finished¦40987 speaking¦40988 to¦40984 \add @Mosheh\add*, he gave¦40983 Mosheh the two¦40992 stone¦40996 slabs with the transcript¦40994 that he had engraved on¦40990 them with his own finger¦40998.
\c 32
\s1 The gold bull idol
\rem /s1 The Gold Bull-Calf; The Golden Calf; The Calf of Gold
\r (Deu. 9:6-29)
\p
\v 1 \add Meanwhile,\add* the people had noticed¦41001 that Mosheh \add ≈had been up on the mountain¦41010 for a long time\add*, \add so\add* \add *they\add* gathered¦41011 themselves around Aharon¦41015 and¦41001 told him, “Come¦41007 on. Make¦41020 \add +some\add* gods¦41023 for us that can go¦41025 ahead of us, because¦41003 we¦41038 don't¦41037 know¦41038 what's happened¦41041 to that Mosheh—the man¦41032\f + \fr 32:1 \ft The way that the people speak of Mosheh here suggests that maybe they never really ever regarded him as being one of them—remember, he did grow up in an Egyptian palace.\f* who¦41033 brought¦41034 us out of Egypt¦41036.”\x + \xo 32:1: \xt Acts 7:40.\x*
\p
\v 2 Aharon¦41046 \add ≈replied\add*, “Go and get the gold¦41049 earrings off your wives¦41052 and your sons¦41053 and daughters¦41054, and bring¦41055 them¦41055 to¦41056 me¦41056.”
\v 3 \add ≈So¦41062\add* the people¦41061 took¦41058 off all their¦41067 gold¦41065 earrings and¦41068 brought¦41068 them¦41068 to¦41069 Aharon¦41071,
\v 4 and he¦41075 took¦41073 them and smelted and crafted the gold into the form of a young bull. Then¦41073 \add @the people\add* said¦41081, “These are¦41083 your¦41083 gods,\f + \fr 32:4 \ft After crafting the gold into the form of a young bull (which wasn't necessarily solid but may have had an internal wooden frame or a clay centre), it's not clear here why the text refers to plural ‘gods’.\f* Yisrael¦41084, who¦41085 brought¦41086 you¦41086 out of Egypt¦41088.”\x + \xo 32:4: \xt 1Ki 12:28; Acts 7:41.\x*
\p
\v 5 \add ≈When¦41090\add* Aharon¦41091 saw¦41090 \add <that\add*, he¦41097 built¦41092 an¦41093 altar¦41093 in front¦41094 of the bull and¦41090 announced, “Tomorrow¦41096 will¦41100 be¦41100 a festival¦41098 to¦41099 \add honour\add* Yahweh¦41099.”
\v 6 \add ≈So¦41102\add* they¦41102 got up early¦41102 the next¦41103 day¦41103 and offered¦41104 burnt¦41105 offerings and brought¦41106 peace¦41107 offerings. Then¦41102 the people¦41109 sat¦41108 down to eat¦41110 and drink¦41111, then¦41102 stood up to \add ≈make merry\add*.\x + \xo 32:6: \xt 1Cor 10:7.\x*
\p
\v 7 Then Yahweh¦41117 \add ≈told\add* Mosheh¦41120, “Go on down¦41123 because¦41124 your¦41126 people¦41126 that¦41127 you¦41128 brought¦41128 out of Egypt¦41130 have¦41125 gone bad—
\v 8 they've quickly¦41133 deviated from¦41134 what I instructed¦41138 them¦41138. They've made¦41139 a metal¦41142 bull for¦41140 themselves and have¦41143 bowed¦41143 down¦41143 to it and sacrificed¦41146 to it and they've said¦41149, ‘Yisrael¦41152, these¦41150 are¦41151 your¦41151 gods¦41151 that¦41137 brought¦41154 you¦41154 out of¦41155 Egypt¦41156.’ ”
\v 9 Then¦41158 Yahweh¦41159 said¦41158 to¦41160 Mosheh¦41162, “I've¦41163 seen¦41163 this¦41167 people¦41169, and¦41158 look, \add ≈they're so stubborn\add*.
\v 10 \add So\add* leave¦41177 me alone¦41177 now and let my¦41181 anger¦41181 rage against them. I¦41185 will destroy¦41183 them and make¦41184 you¦41185 into a great¦41187 nation¦41186.”
\v 11 But¦41189 Mosheh¦41190 pleaded with his¦41195 god¦41195 Yahweh and \add ≈asked\add*, “Yahweh, why¦41197 \add ≈are you angry at¦41201\add* your people¦41201 that¦41202 you have brought¦41203 out¦41203 of¦41204 Egypt¦41205 with \add ≈your incredible power¦41206 and actions\add*?\x + \xo 32:11-14: \xt Num 14:13-19.\x*
\v 12 \add ≈If you did that,\add* the Egyptians would say, ‘\add Ha,\add* he¦41216 brought¦41216 them out¦41216 with¦41215 evil plans to kill¦41217 them in¦41215 the mountains¦41219 and to destroy them from \add ≈off the earth\add*.’ Turn¦41224 from your anger¦41226 and repent from \add any idea of doing\add* evil to your people¦41231.
\v 13 Remember¦41233 Abraham¦41234 and Yitshak¦41235 and Yisra'el¦41236—your servants¦41237 that¦41254 you swore¦41239 to them yourself and told them, ‘I will cause your descendants to increase¦41244 like¦41248 the stars¦41248 in the sky, and I will give¦41256 your descendants all¦41250 this¦41253 land¦41252 which¦41254 I told you about, and they¦41258 will inherit¦41258 it forever.’ ”\x + \xo 32:13: \xt Gen 22:16-17; Gen 17:8.\x*
\v 14 \add So\add* Yahweh¦41262 repented from the¦41265 evil that¦41266 he'd said he'd do¦41268 to¦41269 his¦41269 people¦41269.
\p
\v 15 Then Mosheh¦41274 turned¦41272 and went down the mountain¦41277 carrying the two¦41278 tablets with the transcript¦41280. The tablets were engraved on both¦41278 sides¦41285—front and back.
\v 16 \add *They\add* were God's¦41293 work¦41292—it was¦41296 \add *his\add* writing¦41296 and¦41291 he had inscribed it on¦41300 the¦41302 tablets¦41302.
\v 17 \add As they descended,\add* Yehoshua heard the sounds of people¦41309 shouting¦41310 and¦41312 said¦41312 to Mosheh¦41315, “\add ≈It sounds like a war going on¦41310 down there\add* in¦41310 the camp¦41318!”
\v 18 \add ≈But¦41321\add* \add @Mosheh¦41321\add* \add ≈responded¦41321\add*, “It's not a victory march, and¦41326 it's not \add ≈moans of defeat\add*—it's singing that I can hear¦41333!”
