\v 20 He¦41361 took¦41361 the bull they¦41366 had¦41366 made and burnt¦41367 it in¦41368 the fire¦41368, then¦41361 he ground¦41369 it \add down\add* until¦41370 it was¦41373 powder and sprinkled it on¦41368 top of \add pots of\add* water¦41378 and made the Israelis¦41383 drink¦41379 it.
\p
\v 21 Then¦41385 Mosheh¦41386 \add ≈demanded from\add* Aharon¦41389, “What did¦41392 \add #these\add* people¦41394 do¦41392 to you to make you bring¦41398 such a terrible sin¦41400 on¦41399 them?”
\v 22 Aharon¦41404 \add ≈responded¦41403\add*, “Don't¦41405 \add ≈be angry with¦41416 me\add*, my¦41409 master¦41409. You know¦41411 the¦41414 people¦41414—\add ≈they're intent on¦41416\add* evil¦41416.
\v 23 They¦41419 \add ≈insisted, saying¦41419\add*, ‘Make¦41421 a god for us \add ≈to lead us\add*. As for that Mosheh¦41432—the man¦41433 that brought¦41435 us out of¦41436 Egypt¦41437—we¦41439 don't¦41438 know¦41439 what's¦41440 happened¦41442 to him¦41443.’
\v 24 \add ≈So¦41445\add* I \add ≈told\add* them¦41446, ‘Anyone who has gold¦41448 \add jewellery\add*, take it off¦41449 yourself¦41449,’ and they¦41450 gave¦41450 it to¦41452 me¦41452 and I threw¦41453 it into the fire¦41454, and this¦41457 bull came out.”
\p
\v 25 Mosheh¦41460 saw¦41459 that the people¦41463 \add ≈were out of control¦41469\add* because¦41464 Aharon¦41470 had¦41469 let¦41469 \add ≈them go wild¦41469\add*, \add and now they were subject\add* to mockery \add ≈from any group that stood up\add* against¦41472 them.
\v 26 Then¦41474 Mosheh¦41475 stood¦41474 at¦41476 the camp¦41477 entrance¦41476 and¦41474 \add ≈asked\add*, “Anyone who's¦41479 for¦41480 Yahweh¦41480, \add ≈come\add* to¦41481 me¦41481.” And¦41482 all¦41484 the \add men from the\add* clan of¦41486 Levi¦41487 gathered¦41482 around him.
\v 27 Then¦41489 he¦41489 \add ≈told\add* them¦41490, “This is what Yahweh¦41494, the god¦41495 of Yisrael¦41496, says¦41493: ‘Each man \add ≈must strap\add* his sword¦41500 on¦41508 his side. Pass¦41504 through and return¦41505 from¦41506 gate to¦41507 gate in¦41508 the camp¦41508 and kill¦41509 \add ≈the unfaithful men—even if it's your\add* brother¦41514, or friend, or neighbour¦41518.’ ”
\v 28 The Levite men did¦41524 what Mosheh¦41529 ordered¦41528 and¦41530 they¦41524 killed about¦41536 three¦41536 thousand¦41537 Israeli men that¦41535 day¦41534.
\v 29 Then¦41540 Mosheh¦41541 \add ≈told\add* \add <them\add*, “\add ≈Consecrate yourselves¦41551 to¦41545\add* Yahweh¦41545 today, because¦41546 any man who \add stood\add* against his son¦41548 or his brother¦41549 today \add has\add* placed a blessing¦41553 on¦41548 \add #himself\add*.”
\rem /s1 Moses Intercedes for Israel
\p
\v 30 The¦41556 next¦41556 day¦41556, Mosheh¦41558 \add ≈told\add* the¦41561 people¦41561, “You all have¦41563 committed a terrible sin, \add ≈but¦41555\add* now¦41566 I will¦41567 go¦41567 up¦41567 to¦41568 Yahweh¦41570—perhaps¦41571 I can atone¦41572 for¦41573 your sin.”
\v 31 \add ≈So¦41576\add* Mosheh¦41577 returned¦41576 to¦41578 Yahweh¦41580 and said¦41581, “Please¦41582, \add #these people¦41584 have¦41588\add* committed a terrible sin¦41586 and made¦41588 gods¦41590 for¦41589 themselves out of¦41590 gold¦41591.
\v 32 \add ≈But¦41593\add* now¦41593, \add ≈maybe you'll\add* forgive¦41596 their¦41597 sin¦41597, but¦41593 if not¦41600, please¦41602 blot me¦41601 out¦41601 of¦41603 your¦41603 book¦41603 that¦41604 you've¦41605 written¦41605.”\x + \xo 32:32: \xt Psa 69:28; Rev 3:5.\x*
\v 33 \add ≈But¦41607\add* Yahweh¦41608 said¦41607 to Mosheh¦41611, “It's anyone¦41613 who sinned¦41614 against me¦41616 that I'll¦41617 blot out¦41617 of¦41618 my¦41618 book¦41618.
\v 34 \add ≈So¦41620\add* go now \add and\add* lead¦41623 the people¦41626 to where¦41628 I've¦41630 spoken¦41630 to you. See, my¦41633 angel¦41633 will¦41634 go \add ≈ahead of you, but¦41620\add* on¦41636 the day¦41636 \add ≈that I settle accounts\add*, then¦41620 I'll¦41638 punish them¦41639 for their¦41640 sin¦41640.”
\p
\v 35 Then¦41642 Yahweh¦41643 sent¦41642 \add ≈deadly diseases\add* onto the people¦41646 because they¦41649 had¦41649 got Aharon¦41655 to make the \add gold\add* bull.
\c 33
\s1 God tells them to leave Mt. Sinai
\rem /s1 The Command to Leave Sinai; The Lord Orders Israel to Leave Mount Sinai
\p
\v 1 Then Yahweh¦41659 \add ≈told\add* Mosheh¦41662, “Go \add and\add* pack up¦41664 from¦41665 here¦41665, you and the people¦41667 that you brought¦41669 out of¦41670 Egypt¦41671. Go to the land¦41674 which¦41675 I promised to Abraham¦41677, to Yitshak¦41678, and to Yacob¦41679, \add ≈when I told them that\add* I'd give¦41682 it to \add ≈their descendants¦41681\add*.\x + \xo 33:1: a \xt Gen 12:7; \xo b \xt Gen 26:3; \xo c \xt Gen 28:13.\x*
\v 2 I'll send¦41684 an¦41686 angel¦41686 \add ≈ahead of you\add*, and I'll drive¦41687 out¦41687 the Canaanites¦41690, the Amorites¦41691, the Hittites¦41692, the Perizzites¦41693, the Hivites¦41694, and the Yebusites.
\v 3 \add It's\add* a land¦41699 flowing¦41700 with¦41706 milk¦41701 and¦41702 honey¦41702, but¦41702 I won't¦41704 \add ≈stay among you\add* in¦41706 case I \add decide to\add* destroy¦41716 you on¦41706 the way¦41717 because¦41703 you're \add ≈stubborn\add* people¦41708.”\x + \xo 33:3 \xt 32:9.\x*
\p
