\p
\v 7 \add From that day onwards,\add* Mosheh¦41776 would take¦41777 a tent and¦41776 would put it up at a distance¦41787 outside the camp—he called¦41791 it ‘the tent of meeting’. Then¦41776 anyone¦41798 \add ≈who¦41798 wanted a decision from\add* Yahweh¦41799 would go¦41800 out¦41800 to¦41801 that tent of meeting outside the camp.
\v 8 Whenever Mosheh went out to¦41812 the tent, all¦41816 the people¦41818 would stand¦41819 up at the entrance of their own tents, and¦41809 they¦41823 would watch¦41823 Mosheh go out until¦41826 he went into the tent.
\v 9 Once \add *he\add* entered¦41832 the tent, the pillar¦41836 of cloud¦41837 would come¦41835 down¦41835 and stand¦41838 at the entrance of the tent, and \add @Yahweh\add* would speak¦41841 with¦41842 \add *him¦41844\add*.
\v 10 \add When\add* all¦41847 the people¦41849 saw¦41846 the pillar¦41852 of cloud¦41853 standing¦41854 at the entrance of the tent¦41856, \add *they¦41861\add* would get up and¦41846 bow down¦41861 at the entrance of \add #their\add* \add own\add* \add #tents\add*.
\v 11 Yahweh¦41868 would speak to Mosheh face to face like someone speaks¦41877 to \add #their\add* friend. Then¦41867 Mosheh would return¦41882 to the camp¦41885, but¦41867 his¦41886 servant¦41886 Yehoshua (a young¦41891 man¦41891 who was the son¦41888 of Nun¦41890) would not¦41892 leave the inside¦41894 of the tent¦41895.
\s1 Mosheh sees the master's splendour
\rem /s1 Moses and the Glory of the Lord; Moses Sees the Lord's Glory; The Lord Promises to Be with His People; Moses' Intercession
\p
\v 12 Then Mosheh¦41899 said to Yahweh¦41902, “Listen, you've been saying¦41905 to me, ‘Take \add #these\add* people¦41910 \add ≈onwards\add*,’ but¦41898 you haven't let me know who you'll send¦41918 with¦41923 me, although you have¦41921 said, ‘I know you by¦41923 name¦41923, and¦41924 you've also¦41924 found¦41926 favour¦41927 in¦41923 my¦41928 \add ≈sight¦41928\add*.’
\v 13 \add ≈So¦41930\add* now¦41930 please, if I've¦41934 found¦41934 favour in your \add ≈sight\add*, please \add ≈help\add* me to know your ways¦41941. Then¦41930 I'll know you¦41942 so¦41943 that I can find¦41944 favour in your \add ≈sight\add*. And¦41948 \add don't forget\add* that this nation¦41951 is¦41950 \em your\em* people¦41950.”
\p
\v 14 \add @Yahweh\add* \add ≈replied\add*, “My¦41955 \add ≈presence¦41955\add* will go¦41956 \add with you\add* and¦41957 I will \add ≈help\add* you \add to be able to\add* rest¦41957.”
\p
\v 15 \add @Mosheh\add* \add ≈replied\add* to¦41961 him¦41961, “If¦41962 your¦41965 \add ≈presence¦41965\add* isn't¦41964 \add ≈coming with us\add*, then¦41960 don't¦41964 \add ≈make us leave\add* here¦41970.
\v 16 \add ≈How would anyone know¦41974\add* that I've¦41978 found¦41978 favour¦41979 in your \add ≈sight¦41980\add*—me and your people \add that is\add*—if you didn't¦41983 \add ≈come\add* with¦41972 us¦41985? \add ≈How could\add* I and your people be distinguished¦41986 from¦41990 all¦41990 the \add other\add* people \add groups\add* \add ≈in the world\add*?”
\p
\v 17 Yahweh¦42001 \add ≈replied\add* to¦42002 Mosheh¦42004, “\add Okay,\add* I'll¦42012 also¦42005 do¦42012 \add ≈what you've asked\add* because¦42013 you've found¦42015 favour¦42016 in¦42017 my¦42017 \add ≈sight¦42017\add* and¦42018 I know¦42018 you by name¦42019.”
\p
\v 18 Then¦42021 \add @Mosheh\add*, “Please¦42024 show¦42022 me¦42022 your¦42026 splendour¦42026.”
\p
\v 19 Yahweh \add ≈replied\add*, “I myself will cause¦42030 all¦42031 my goodness¦42033 to pass¦42030 over \add ≈in front of you\add*, and I will \add ≈say¦42028\add* \add *my\add* name¦42038 of Yahweh \add ≈in front of you\add*. I will favour¦42045 \add ≈anyone I want\add*, and I'll¦42030 be compassionate to \add ≈whoever I want\add*.”\x + \xo 33:19: \xt Rom 9:15.\x*
\v 20 \add ≈But¦42052\add* he¦42052 said¦42052, “You¦42056 won't¦42053 be¦42054 able¦42054 to see my¦42058 face¦42058, because¦42059 no human¦42063 can see me¦42062 and¦42052 \add still\add* live¦42064.”
\v 21 \add *He¦42068\add* \add ≈continued¦42066\add*, “Look¦42067, there's a place¦42069 near me¦42070 where you¦42071 can \add ≈stand¦42071 there\add* on¦42072 the¦42074 rock¦42074.
\v 22 Then¦42076 while my splendour¦42078 passes¦42077 over, I'll¦42079 put¦42079 you in a crevice in the rock¦42081, and¦42076 my hand¦42083 will cover¦42082 you until¦42085 I've¦42087 gone past.
\v 23 Then¦42089 I'll¦42089 take my hand¦42092 away and¦42089 you'll be able to see¦42093 my back¦42096, but¦42089 \add ≈you mustn't try to look at\add* my face¦42097.”
\c 34
\s1 The replacement stone slabs
\rem /s1 A New Copy of the Covenant; The Second Set of Stone Tablets; The New Stone Tablets; Moses Makes New Tablets
\r (Deu. 10:1-5)
\p
\v 1 Then Yahweh¦42103 \add ≈continued¦42102\add* speaking to Mosheh¦42106, “Carve two¦42110 slabs of stone¦42113 for yourself¦42109 just like¦42114 the first \add >ones\add*. Then the words¦42121 that were¦42123 on the first tablets¦42126 that you¦42129 broke¦42129, I'll¦42115 write¦42115 them \add again\add* on the slabs.
\v 2 Be¦42131 ready by morning, and in¦42135 the morning come¦42134 up to Mt¦42138. Sinai¦42139, and present¦42140 yourself¦42140 there¦42142 to me¦42141 up on¦42135 the top¦42145.
\v 3 Don't¦42149 bring anyone with¦42152 you¦42152, and also¦42153 don't let anyone be¦42158 on the mountain at all—don't even let their flocks¦42164 and herds¦42165 graze¦42168 \add ≈at the base\add* of¦42172 that mountain.”
\v 4 \add ≈So¦42175\add* \add @Mosheh¦42182\add* carved out¦42175 two slabs of stone like¦42180 the first¦42180 \add >ones\add*, and \add *he¦42181\add* got up early¦42181 in¦42183 the morning¦42183 and went up to¦42185 Mt¦42182. Sinai¦42188 as¦42189 Yahweh¦42191 had¦42190 commanded¦42190 him¦42192, carrying up the two slabs of stone.
\v 5 Then¦42199 Yahweh came down in¦42201 the cloud¦42201 and stood¦42202 with¦42201 him¦42203 there¦42204, and he¦42205 pronounced \add ≈his\add* name¦42206 ‘Yahweh’.
\v 6 Yahweh passed¦42209 over above his¦42214 face¦42214 and proclaimed, “I am Yahweh, a compassionate¦42220 and gracious¦42221 God¦42219, \add ≈slow to get angry but¦42209 exuding\add* faithfulness¦42227 and trustworthiness.\x + \xo 34:6-7: \xt Exo 20:5-6; Num 14:18; Deu 5:9-10; 7:9-10.\x*
\v 7 \add I\add* display faithfulness to thousands¦42232 \add ?of generations\add*—forgiving¦42233 disobedience, transgression¦42235, and sin¦42236. But¦42235 \add ≈I\add* certainly¦42237 won't¦42238 let the guilty \add ≈get away with it\add*—visiting¦42240 the iniquity¦42234 of the \add ≈parents¦42243\add* onto the \add ≈children¦42250\add* and onto the \add ≈grandchildren\add*—to the third¦42253 and the fourth¦42256 \add generations\add*.”
\p
\v 8 Mosheh¦42259 hurried¦42258 and bowed¦42260 to the ground and worshipped¦42262 \add <Yahweh\add*
\v 9 and said¦42264, “Please¦42267, if¦42265 I¦42268 have¦42268 found¦42268 favour¦42269 in¦42270 your \add ≈sight¦42270\add*, my master¦42271, please¦42274 go¦42272 with¦42270 us, because¦42277 \add #these\add* are \add ≈stubborn\add* people¦42278. And¦42284 forgive¦42284 our disobedience and our sin¦42286 and \add ≈take¦42287 us as¦42287 your inheritance\add*.”
\rem /s1 The Covenant Is Renewed; The Covenant Renewed
\rem /r (Exodus 23.14-19; Deuteronomy 7.1-5; 16.1-17)
\p
\v 10 \add @Yahweh¦42321\add* said¦42289, “Listen, I'm about¦42292 to make¦42292 an agreement¦42293 in front of all your people.\f + \fr 34:10 \ft Because there's no punctuation in the original Hebrew, it's not certain if ‘in front of all your people’ goes with what it follows (as the \+em OET-RV\+em* has chosen), or with what follows it (as in several other translations).\f* I will do miracles that have¦42303 not been¦42303 \add ≈done before¦42294\add* anywhere on¦42304 the earth¦42306 or in any country \add of the world\add*. All the people that you're¦42316 among will see¦42310 \add *my\add* work¦42320, because¦42322 what I'm going to do with you is \add ≈awe-inspiring\add*.
\v 11 \add ≈Be sure to obey\add* what I'm telling you today. See, I'm about¦42340 to force the Amorites¦42344, the Canaanites¦42345, the Hittites¦42346, the Perizzites¦42347, the Hivites¦42348, and the Yebusites out of the land ahead of you.
\v 12 \add ≈Be very careful\add* not to make¦42355 any treaties with¦42367 any of the \add current\add* inhabitants¦42357 of the land¦42358 that¦42359 you're¦42360 about¦42361 to enter, in¦42367 case it ends up trapping you.
\v 13 \add ≈What you must¦42373 do instead is to\add* break¦42377 down their altars¦42372 and smash¦42377 their pillars¦42376, and cut¦42381 down the poles¦42380 \add used to worship their god\add* Asherah¦42380.\x + \xo 34:13: \xt Deu 16:21.\x*
\v 14 You¦42385 must¦42385 not¦42384 bow¦42385 down¦42385 to any other god¦42386 because¦42388 Yahweh¦42389 is¦42390 a jealous God¦42386—jealous \add to protect\add* his name¦42391.
\v 15 So don't make¦42398 an agreement¦42399 with the \add #inhabitants¦42400\add* of the land¦42401, \add because when\add* they prostitute¦42402 \add <themselves¦42402\add* to their gods¦42405 and sacrifice to \add *them\add*, and then \add #they\add* invite¦42408 you \add to join them\add* and you eat¦42410 some¦42411 of \add #their\add* sacrifice,
\v 16 then \add you'll end up by\add* allowing your sons to marry their daughters¦42417 who'll prostitute¦42416 \add <themselves\add* to their gods¦42419, and¦42413 then your sons \add ≈will do the same\add*.
\p
\v 17 Don't¦42429 make¦42430 cast metal¦42428 gods¦42427 for¦42432 yourselves¦42432.\x + \xo 34:17: \xt Exo 20:4; Lev 19:4; Deu 5:8; 27:15.\x*
\p
\v 18 You must observe the Flat Bread Celebration \add every year\add* as I instructed¦42444 you. For seven¦42439 days¦42440 you must eat¦42441 \add only\add* bread¦42437 that hasn't been risen, at¦42449 the appointed¦42445 time¦42445 in¦42449 late March or early April because¦42448 that's when you came¦42451 out¦42451 of Egypt¦42452.\x + \xo 34:18: \xt Exo 12:14-20; Lev 23:6-8; Num 28:16-25.\x*
\v 19 All¦42459 of¦42461 your eldest male offspring belong to¦42458 me¦42458, \add including your sons\add* and the¦42463 first males born from your cattle and sheep¦42465 and goats.\x + \xo 34:19: \xt Exo 13:2.\x*
\v 20 If it's a male donkey, a lamb can be given as a ransom instead, but¦42467 if¦42471 you don't¦42473 pay a ransom then¦42467 you must¦42469 kill the¦42477 donkey. \add ≈It's compulsory to\add* ransom your¦42478 eldest sons¦42478. \add ≈Don't¦42473 come to worship me without bringing something\add*.\x + \xo 34:20: \xt Exo 13:13.\x*
\p
\v 21 \add Each week,\add* you should only work for six days¦42487, then you must¦42488 rest¦42491 on¦42489 the¦42492 seventh¦42490 day¦42489—\add even\add* during ploughing and¦42493 harvest¦42493 times.\x + \xo 34:21: \xt Exo 20:9-10; 23:12; 31:15; 35:2; Lev 23:3; Deu 5:13-14.\x*
\p
\v 22 \add In the spring\add* when you begin to¦42499 harvest¦42501 the first¦42500 wheat¦42502 crop, you must¦42498 have a \it Celebration of Weeks\it*, and¦42496 at the end of the year¦42506 \add in the autumn\add*, have a \it \+add Finished\+add* Harvest¦42501 Celebration\it*.\x + \xo 34:22: a \xt Exo 23:16; Lev 23:15-21; Num 28:26-31; \xo b \xt Lev 23:39-43.\x*
\p
\v 23 Three¦42508 times¦42509 every¦42512 year¦42510, all your¦42514 men must¦42511 present¦42511 themselves before me—Isra'el's¦42522 god¦42521, the master¦42518 Yahweh¦42520.
\v 24 I will drive out the people groups ahead of you and expand your borders, and no one will \add ≈think of taking\add* your land¦42539 \add when they know that\add* you present¦42544 yourselves¦42541 to¦42541 \add *me\add* three¦42547 times¦42548 a year¦42549.
\p
\v 25 Don't \add wave bread\add* \add ≈that's been risen\add* when offering a sacrifice. Don't allow any part of¦42559 the sacrifice for the ‘pass-over¦42566’ celebration to \add ≈still be there in\add* the morning¦42563.\x + \xo 34:25: \xt Exo 12:10.\x*
\p
\v 26 You¦42573 must¦42571 bring¦42571 the best of the first¦42568 parts of your¦42570 harvests to \add *my\add* residence.\x + \xo 34:26: a \xt Deu 26:2; \xo b \xt Deu 14:21.\x*
\p Don't¦42575 boil¦42577 a young goat in¦42579 its¦42580 mother's¦42580 milk¦42579.
\p
\v 27 Yahweh¦42584 \add ≈told\add* Mosheh¦42587, “Write¦42588 down these words for yourself¦42590, because¦42595 \add ≈it's in accordance with\add* these words that I've¦42602 made¦42602 an agreement¦42604 with you¦42603 and¦42605 with Yisrael¦42607.”
\v 28 \add @Mosheh\add* was¦42609 there¦42611 with¦42612 Yahweh¦42614 for forty¦42615 days and nights¦42618, and \add during that time\add* he didn't¦42620 eat¦42621 or \add even\add* drink water¦42622, and he wrote¦42625 the ten¦42632 commands¦42633 of¦42630 the agreement¦42631 on the \add stone\add* slabs.
\rem /s1 The Shining Face of Moses; Moses Goes Down from Mount Sinai; The Radiant Face of Moses
\p
\v 29 \add ≈So¦42635 when¦42636\add* Mosheh¦42637 came¦42636 down¦42636 from¦42638 Mt¦42649. Sinai¦42639, he was carrying the two¦42640 \add stone\add* slabs with the transcript¦42642 \add of the ten commands\add*, \add ≈but¦42635\add* what he didn't¦42651 know¦42653 as he descended was that¦42654 the skin¦42656 on¦42636 his face¦42657 was shining¦42655 after his talking¦42658 with \add @Yahweh\add*.\x + \xo 34:29-35: \xt 2Cor 3:7-16.\x*
\v 30 \add ≈When¦42667\add* Aharon¦42662 and the Israelis¦42666 saw¦42661 Mosheh¦42669, wow, \add ≈his¦42673 face¦42673 radiated light\add* and they¦42674 were¦42674 afraid¦42674 to go close to him¦42676.
\v 31 \add ≈But¦42678\add* Mosheh¦42680 called¦42678 them \add over\add*, and Aharon¦42683 and all¦42684 of the¦42686 community¦42687 leaders¦42686 returned¦42681 back to¦42682 him¦42682, and \add *he¦42688\add* spoke¦42688 with¦42687 them.
\v 32 After¦42692 that, the Israelis¦42699 came closer, and¦42700 \add @Mosheh\add* gave them¦42700 all¦42702 the instructions¦42700 that Yahweh¦42706 had¦42705 told¦42700 him¦42707 on¦42708 Mt¦42708. Sinai¦42709.
\v 33 \add ≈Then¦42712 when\add* \add *he'd\add* finished¦42711 talking¦42713 to them¦42714, \add @Mosheh¦42712\add* put a veil¦42719 over¦42716 his¦42718 face¦42718,
\v 34 and¦42721 whenever \add *he\add* would go¦42721 in¦42721 to speak¦42725 with¦42721 Yahweh¦42724, he would remove¦42727 the veil¦42730 until¦42731 he came¦42733 out. \add ≈Whenever¦42722\add* he did come out, he'd tell the Israelis¦42739 what he'd been instructed¦42742,
\v 35 and¦42744 \add *they¦42744\add* would see¦42744 how \add *his\add* face shone¦42753. Then¦42744 Mosheh¦42751 would put¦42757 the veil¦42761 back¦42757 over¦42762 his face until¦42765 he¦42767 went¦42767 in \add the next time\add* to¦42768 speak¦42768 with¦42769 \add @Yahweh\add*.
\c 35
\s1 Instructions for the rest day
