\p
\v 1 Mosheh¦42773 assembled¦42772 all¦42776 the Israelis¦42780 and¦42781 told¦42787 them¦42782, “These¦42783 are¦42784 the things¦42784 that¦42785 Yahweh¦42788 has¦42787 instructed¦42787 you to¦42789 do¦42789.
\v 2 \add Every week\add*, you can work¦42795 for six days¦42793, but¦42796 the seventh¦42797 day will be a sacred¦42800 rest day, \add dedicated to\add* Yahweh¦42803. Anyone¦42806 who¦42806 works on¦42796 that day must¦42794 be put¦42809 to death¦42809.\x + \xo 35:2: \xt Exo 20:8-11; 23:12; 31:15; 34:21; Lev 23:3; Deu 5:12-14.\x*
\v 3 Don't light a fire¦42814\f + \fr 35:3 \ft This is effectively a command not to do any \+bd cooking\+bd* on the rest day.\f* in¦42815 any of your¦42816 homes on the rest days.”
\s1 The offering for Yahweh
